## Example

### Input

```text
*...
....
.*..
....
```

### Output

```text
*100
2210
1*10
1110
```

### Explanation

* Cell (0,1) has one adjacent mine.
* Cell (1,0) has two adjacent mines.
* Cell (2,1) contains a mine.
* Remaining cells display the number of surrounding mines.

This problem is widely used in competitive programming because it teaches matrix traversal and efficient implementation of neighbor-search algorithms.

